{
  "email": "hannah.lee@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports temporary onboarding password rejected at forced change; checking account status and must_change_password per KB-003."
}

{
  "user_id": 12,
  "reason": "Checking recent sign-in attempts and results for the forced password change failures (KB-003 quick checks, network type)."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, your account is active and is set to require a new password at your next sign-in, so the temporary password itself is being recognized. To set the new password, please try these steps: 1) Sign in on your laptop's Windows sign-in screen (not a web page), while connected to the office network or VPN. 2) Check that Caps Lock is off and that your keyboard is set to the usual language. 3) Choose a new password of at least 14 characters that you haven't used before. If you still get an error, please reply with the exact error message, the time you tried, and whether you were on the office network, VPN, or home Wi-Fi, and we'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user for user 12 (Hannah Lee, Finance, not VIP). Account active, not blocked, failed_login_count 0, must_change_password true, password_last_set 2026-10-11. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days show 10 successes (corporate and VPN from residential IP) and zero failed_password results, so the failed attempts from the ticket are not appearing in the logs. That is worth noting if this continues. KB-003 escalation condition (active, no change required, no password works) does not apply because must_change_password is true. No reset or unlock was requested or needed. Next step: user to retry on the Windows sign-in screen on VPN/office network with the 14-character rule; if the error persists with the exact message, escalate to Tier 2 and check why the change attempts are not logged. Fallback per KB-003 step 4 is a new temporary password via KB-002 (needs tech approval, delivered by phone).",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-003",
    "KB-002"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
